cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these results, please cite the paper and this software deposit."
title: "Code and results for: Location bias and encoding geometry in metaheuristic benchmarks for cardinality-constrained portfolio optimization"
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
type: software
abstract: >-
  Python code, raw results, exact reference solutions (SCIP) and figures of a study of
  location bias and encoding geometry in metaheuristic benchmarks for the
  cardinality-constrained mean-variance portfolio problem on the OR-Library instances
  port1-port5. Includes reflected-encoding controls, a five-location test on test
  functions, and eleven optimizers (GWO, HHO, WOA, SCA, PSO, DE, GA, L-SHADE,
  BIPOP-CMA-ES, ESDO and ESDO-R).
keywords:
  - portfolio optimization
  - cardinality constraint
  - metaheuristics
  - benchmarking
  - structural bias
  - mixed-integer quadratic programming
authors:
